    {
      "id": "net-delta-serialize",
      "name": "NetDeltaSerialize",
      "category": "NetSerialization",
      "signature": "NetDeltaSerialize(Delta Parms)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Delta Parms",
          "type": "FNetDeltaSerializeInfo&"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "Bool",
      "docs": "@param DeltaParms\tGeneric struct of input parameters for delta serialization\n@return return true if the serialization was fully mapped. If false, the property will be considered 'dirty' and will replicate again on the next update.\nThis is needed for UActor* properties. If an actor's Actorchannel is not fully mapped, properties referencing it must stay dirty.\nNote that UPackageMap::SerializeObject returns false if an object is unmapped. Generally, you will want to return false from your ::NetSerialize\nif you make any calls to ::SerializeObject that return false."
    },
