    {
      "id": "safe-net-serialize-t-array-header-only",
      "name": "SafeNetSerializeTArray_HeaderOnly",
      "category": "NetSerialization",
      "signature": "SafeNetSerializeTArray_HeaderOnly<T, A>(Ar, Array, Out Success)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Ar",
          "type": "FArchive&"
        },
        {
          "name": "Array",
          "type": "TArray<T,A>&"
        },
        {
          "name": "Out Success",
          "type": "Bool&"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "template<int32 MaxNum,T,A> int32",
      "docs": "===================== Safe TArray Serialization =====================\nThese are helper methods intended to make serializing TArrays safer in custom\n::NetSerialize functions. These enforce max limits on array size, so that a malformed\npacket is not able to allocate an arbitrary amount of memory (E.g., a hacker serilizes\na packet where a TArray size is of size MAX_int32, causing gigs of memory to be allocated for\nthe TArray).\nThese should only need to be used when you are overriding ::NetSerialize on a UStruct via struct traits.\nWhen using default replication, TArray properties already have this built in security.\nSafeNetSerializeTArray_Default - calls << operator to serialize the items in the array.\nSafeNetSerializeTArray_WithNetSerialize - calls NetSerialize to serialize the items in the array.\nWhen saving, bOutSuccess will be set to false if the passed in array size exceeds to MaxNum template parameter.\nExample:\nFMyStruct {\nTArray<float>\t\t\t\t\t\tMyFloats;\t\t// We want to call << to serialize floats\nTArray<FVector_NetQuantizeNormal>\tMyVectors;\t\t// We want to call NetSeriailze on these *\nbool NetSerialize(FArchive& Ar, class UPackageMap* Map, bool& bOutSuccess)\n{\n// Don't do this:\nAr << MyFloats;\nAr << MyVectors;\n// Do this instead:\nSafeNetSerializeTArray_Default<31>(Ar, MyFloats);\nSafeNetSerializeTArray_WithNetSerialize<31>(Ar, MyVectors, Map);\n}\n}"
    },
    {
      "id": "safe-net-serialize-t-array-default",
      "name": "SafeNetSerializeTArray_Default",
      "category": "NetSerialization",
      "signature": "SafeNetSerializeTArray_Default<T, A>(Ar, Array)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Ar",
          "type": "FArchive&"
        },
        {
          "name": "Array",
          "type": "TArray<T,A>&"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "template<int32 MaxNum,T,A> bool"
    },
    {
      "id": "safe-net-serialize-t-array-with-net-serialize",
      "name": "SafeNetSerializeTArray_WithNetSerialize",
      "category": "NetSerialization",
      "signature": "SafeNetSerializeTArray_WithNetSerialize<T, A>(Ar, Array, Package Map)",
      "params": [
